Reference material (not distributed, not compiled):

  The circuit and its values come from the schematic traced by Kit Rae
  (BigMuffPage) and are transcribed in docs/netlist.md, cross-checked against
  ElectroSmash's "Big Muff Pi Analysis". The solver follows published analysis:

    - D. T. Yeh, "Digital Implementation of Musical Distortion Circuits by
      Analysis and Simulation", PhD thesis, Stanford, 2009 (sec. 4.5, the DK
      method)
    - M. Holters and U. Zolzer, DAFx-11 (pots as variable parts)
    - M. Holters and U. Zolzer, EUSIPCO 2015 (the generalised DK derivation)

  The device parameters in docs/spice/ and src/dsp/circuit/Netlist.h are the
  published BC547C (Philips) and 1N914 (onsemi) SPICE model values, taken from
  the LTspice standard library.

  docs/circuit-model.md compares the engine against a NAM capture, rendered with
  NeuralAmpModelerCore (MIT). Neither is part of this project.

  No source code from any of these is present, apart from the ngspice limiter
  credited above.

